  "result": "Excellent! I've successfully implemented the credit notes functionality. Here's what was added:\n\n**Created `src/credits.js`** with:\n- `createCreditNote(invoice, { amount, reason, date }, existingNumbers)` function that:\n  - Validates invoice status is 'issued', 'partially_paid', or 'paid' (returns NOT_ISSUED for draft)\n  - Validates amount is a positive integer (returns AMOUNT_INVALID for zero, negative, or fractional)\n  - Validates amount doesn't exceed invoice total (returns CREDIT_TOO_HIGH if exceeded)\n  - Returns `ok(creditNote)` with: { number, invoiceNumber, customerId, amount, reason, date }\n  - Uses separate credit note numbering: CN-<year>-<counter> (e.g., CN-2026-0001)\n  - Maintains independent counter from invoice numbers\n  - Uses the date's year for the credit note number prefix\n\n**Updated `src/errors.js`**:\n- Added CREDIT_TOO_HIGH error code\n\n**Created comprehensive test suite (`test/credits.test.js`)** with 20 tests covering:\n- Credit notes for issued, partially_paid, and paid invoices\n- Draft invoice rejection\n- Amount validation (zero, negative, fractional, too high)\n- Maximum valid amount (equal to invoice total)\n- Separate invoice and credit note numbering\n- Year boundary handling\n- Multiple credit notes with correct sequencing\n- Reason tracking\n- Counter padding with zeros\n- Filtering of non-matching numbers\n\n**All 232 tests pass** (20 new credit note tests + 212 existing tests)\n\nThe credit notes system correctly generates unique numbers per year, maintains separate counters from invoices, and enforces all business rules for valid refunds.",
